// impressions. Course thesis: modern technologies and markets are
// industrial-scale phantasia machines — systems engineered to present false
// impressions of the good faster and more persistently than an untrained
// prohairesis can examine them. The Stoic response is not retreat but
// trained assent: the same doctrine, harder conditions.
// Mirrors the PHIL 702 architecture; session 9 is the capstone dialogue.
// Sessions align with phil707_reading.ts. Prerequisites: PHIL 705
// (impressions/assent machinery); PHIL 706 recommended for Sessions 3 and 6.
// The capstone requires a completed, logged fasting protocol (s8) — the
// first course where completion requires lived time, not just dialogue.

